sorry, this isn't what I meant.

currently, in master, we iterate over two distinct sets of file paths, one for possible jsonconfig files, then one for old config files.

I don't think we should combine those into a single list... what if an old config file unmarshalled into a jsonconfig struct without erroring, but also dropped data in the process?

decomposing into functions like this would make them reusable externally without changing the current behavior at all:

```
// ReadDockerConfigFile delegates to ReadDockerConfigJSONFile() and ReadDockercfgFile() using the default search paths
ReadDockerConfigFile() (cfg DockerConfig, err error)

// ReadDockercfgFile attempts to read a legacy dockercfg file from the given paths.
// if searchPaths is empty, the default paths are used.
ReadDockercfgFile(searchPaths []string) (cfg DockerConfig, err error)
DefaultDockercfgPaths() []string

// DefaultDockerConfigJSONPaths attempts to read a docker config.json file from the given paths.
// if searchPaths is empty, the default paths are used.
DefaultDockerConfigJSONPaths() []string
ReadDockerConfigJSONFile(searchPaths []string) (cfg DockerConfig, err error)
```

